  "_id": "tg-die",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "eatest thereof thou shalt surely die, Gen. 2:17 (Moses 3:17). said unto the woman, Ye shall not surely die, Gen. 3:4 (Moses 4:10). firstborn in the land of Egypt shall die, Ex. 11:5. hast thou taken us away to die in the wilderness, Ex. 14:11 (Num. 21:5). let not God speak with us, lest we die, Ex. 20:19. They shall surely die in the wilderness, Num. 26:65. therefore why should we die, Deut. 5:25. even that prophet shall die, Deut. 18:20. one of them die, and have no child, Deut. 25:5 (Matt. 22:24; Mark 12:19; Luke 20:28). Moses … died there, Deut. 34:5. Where thou diest, will I die, Ruth 1:17. Absalom! would God I had died for thee, 2 Sam. 18:33. fathers shall not die for the children, 2 Chr. 25:4. wise men die, likewise the fool, Ps. 49:10. preserve … those that are appointed to die, Ps. 79:11. ye shall die like men, Ps. 82:7. fools die for want of wisdom, Prov. 10:21. he that hateth reproof shall die, Prov. 15:10. time to be born, and a time to die, Eccl. 3:2. why shouldest thou die before thy time, Eccl. 7:17. for to morrow we shall die, Isa. 22:13 (1 Cor. 15:32). child shall die an hundred years old, Isa. 65:20. their worm shall not die, Isa. 66:24 (Mark 9:44, 46, 48). great and the small shall die, Jer. 16:6. every one shall die for his own iniquity, Jer. 31:30. shall not die for the iniquity of his father, Ezek. 18:17. why will ye die, O house of Israel, Ezek. 18:31 (33:11). better for me to die than to live, Jonah 4:3 (4:8).",
